wvkbd-gbook — on-screen keyboard with a Korean layer for the Galaxy Book bundle

wvkbd-gbook is wvkbd 0.15 (Debian forky source, layout "mobintl") built with
wvkbd-0.15-gbook.patch:

  * layer "korean": the full layout with 2-set Hangul labels. It sends the same
    key codes as the Latin layer; fcitx5 (hangul) composes the syllables.
  * key "한/영" on both layers: sends the Hangul key (toggles the input method
    in fcitx5) and switches the labels at once.
  * key "▼" (hide, last key of the bottom row on the Latin, Korean, special
    and nav layers; space key one unit narrower): hides the keyboard like
    SIGUSR1 and sends nothing to the application. gbook-osk-auto shows it again
    at the next text focus (added 2026-11-11: the keyboard stayed on screen and
    the panel toggle was hard to hit by touch).
  * visibility file $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wvkbd-gbook.visible ("1"/"0", written
    on show/hide): gbook-osk-auto shows the keyboard again when a focused
    field is tapped while the keyboard is hidden.
  * signals SIGRTMIN+1 (Latin labels) and SIGRTMIN+2 (Korean labels):
    gbook-osk-auto sends them so that the labels follow the input method even
    when it is switched somewhere else (keyboard cover, tray icon, other
    window).

Rebuild (Debian forky, e.g. in a chroot):

  apt-get install gcc make pkg-config libc6-dev libwayland-dev \
      libxkbcommon-dev libpango1.0-dev wayland-protocols
  apt-get source wvkbd            # or wvkbd_0.15.orig.tar.xz from the pool
  cd wvkbd-0.15 && patch -p1 < ../wvkbd-0.15-gbook.patch && make clean && make
  strip wvkbd-mobintl && cp wvkbd-mobintl wvkbd-gbook

The binary in this directory was built that way on 2026-11-11 on the tablet (amd64;
`make clean` is needed after layout changes — the Makefile does not track the layout header for main.o) and
needs the libraries of the Debian package wvkbd (libwayland-client0,
libpangocairo-1.0-0, libcairo2).
